  data: {
    LLM: "In the kitty, seek cards that complement your hand (completing suits or adding bowers). Bid conservatively early; trust your partner's bids. Always follow suit. If high bidder, play trump cards to establish who holds what.\n\n**Bid Calculation**: Count sure tricks + tricks your partner likely has from their bid signals. A 6-trick bid requires only 6/10 tricks (60% win rate); 10-trick requires 10/10 (100%). **Bower Recognition**: If you hold Left Bower, remember Right Bower is still higher in trump. **No Trump Strategy**: Be cautious; without trump, your Ace is no longer highestâ€”opponents' cards block you easily.\n\n**Bid Communication**: Your bid signals your hand strength. Conservative bids suggest weak hands; aggressive bids suggest strong trump holdings. Partners interpret bids to guide their play. **Counting Out**: Track which high cards have been played to calculate remaining trick probabilities. **Misere Play**: Requires exceptional discipline. Avoid taking any tricks and don't play bower cards.",
    Player: "In the kitty, seek cards that complement your hand (completing suits or adding bowers). Bid conservatively early; trust your partner's bids. Always follow suit. If high bidder, play trump cards to establish who holds what.\n\n**Bid Calculation**: Count sure tricks + tricks your partner likely has from their bid signals. A 6-trick bid requires only 6/10 tricks (60% win rate); 10-trick requires 10/10 (100%). **Bower Recognition**: If you hold Left Bower, remember Right Bower is still higher in trump. **No Trump Strategy**: Be cautious; without trump, your Ace is no longer highestâ€”opponents' cards block you easily.\n\n**Bid Communication**: Your bid signals your hand strength. Conservative bids suggest weak hands; aggressive bids suggest strong trump holdings. Partners interpret bids to guide their play. **Counting Out**: Track which high cards have been played to calculate remaining trick probabilities. **Misere Play**: Requires exceptional discipline. Avoid taking any tricks and don't play bower cards.",
