    basic: "In the kitty, seek cards that complement your hand (completing suits or adding bowers). Bid conservatively early; trust your partner's bids. Always follow suit. If high bidder, play trump cards to establish who holds what.",
    intermediate: "**Bid Calculation**: Count sure tricks + tricks your partner likely has from their bid signals. A 6-trick bid requires only 6/10 tricks (60% win rate); 10-trick requires 10/10 (100%). **Bower Recognition**: If you hold Left Bower, remember Right Bower is still higher in trump. **No Trump Strategy**: Be cautious; without trump, your Ace is no longer highestâ€”opponents' cards block you easily.",
    advanced: "**Bid Communication**: Your bid signals your hand strength. Conservative bids suggest weak hands; aggressive bids suggest strong trump holdings. Partners interpret bids to guide their play. **Counting Out**: Track which high cards have been played to calculate remaining trick probabilities. **Misere Play**: Requires exceptional discipline. Avoid taking any tricks and don't play bower cards.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Early in a bid, save low trump cards (7s, 8s) for later tricks when bowers are exhausted.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If partner bids 8, they likely hold strong trump. Don't compete unless you also have exceptional trump length.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'In No Trump, Aces are valuable but not invincible. Track where high cards land.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Always communicate through your bid. Overbidding signals strength; underbidding signals weakness.',
